/-!
# Global generation of twists by an ample line bundle

Let `X` be a quasi-compact scheme, `L` an ample invertible sheaf on `X`, and `F` a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module of finite type. Serre's twisting-generation theorem states that for all
sufficiently large `n : ℕ`, the twisted sheaf `F ⊗ L^{⊗ n}` is generated by finitely many global
sections (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_isAmple`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensor_of_isAmple` for any line bundle
representing `L^{⊗ n}`). Equivalently, `F` receives an epimorphism from a finite direct sum of
copies of `L^{⊗ (-n)}` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_biproduct_of_isAmple`).

The proof follows Hartshorne, Theorem II.5.17, and the Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3:

* The nonvanishing locus of a positive tensor power `sᵏ` of a section `s` of an invertible sheaf
  equals the nonvanishing locus of `s` (`Scheme.Modules.nonvanishingLocus_tensorPowSection`).
  Using quasi-compactness, ampleness of `L` yields a single positive integer `d` and finitely many
  global sections of `L^{⊗ d}` whose nonvanishing loci are affine and cover `X`
  (`LineBundleClass.IsAmple.exists_pos_tensorPow_finite_affine_cover_nonvanishingLocus`).
* When global sections `s₁, …, sₘ` of an invertible sheaf `M` have affine nonvanishing loci `Uᵢ`
  covering `X`, `Scheme.Modules.eventually_exists_generatingSections_tensor_tensorPow` gives finite
  global generation of `F ⊗ M^{⊗ n}` for all sufficiently large `n`.
* Applying this to the finitely many twists `F ⊗ L^{⊗ r}` (`0 ≤ r < d`) and `M = L^{⊗ d}` yields
  finite global generation for all `n` above a uniform threshold.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.AlgebraicGeometry.LineBundleClass.IsAmple.`
  `exists_pos_tensorPow_finite_affine_cover_nonvanishingLocus`: an ample line bundle has a positive
  power with finitely many global sections whose nonvanishing loci are affine and cover `X`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensorPow_of_isAmple` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_generatingSections_tensor_of_isAmple`: Serre's
  twisting-generation theorem for ample line bundles.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exists_epi_biproduct_of_isAmple`: every finite-type
  quasi-coherent module is a quotient of a finite direct sum of copies of `L^{⊗ (-n)}` for `n ≫ 0`.

## References

* R. Hartshorne, *Algebraic Geometry*, GTM 52, Springer, 1977, Theorem II.5.17.
* [The Stacks Project, Tag 01Q3](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01Q3) (global generation
  after twisting by an ample invertible sheaf).
-/

public section

